DETAIL:  The statement would drop trigger pg_repack_safe_rewrites_protected on table pg_repack_safe_rewrites. A snapshot taken before a recorded REPACK (CONCURRENTLY), on this server or on any standby, would then read the rewritten table as empty.
HINT:  Delete the records with pg_repack_safe_prune_records() and run VACUUM on the record table until it is empty (see the README, "Removing the extension"). A superuser can set pg_repack_safe.allow_unprotected_drop instead.
